{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Sānu","html":"<article id='thag1.44'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 1.44 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 1.44 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Pañcamavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Five </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Sānuttheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sānu </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Mataṁ vā amma rodanti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Mum, they weep for the dead, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yo vā jīvaṁ na dissati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>or for one who’s alive but missing. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Jīvantaṁ maṁ amma passantī, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I’m alive and you can see me, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Kasmā maṁ amma rodasī”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>so mum, why do you weep for me? </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Sānutthero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
